# v29 OVERLAY (user 2026-10-31, "Do it"): v28 with ONE change -- route progress
# is PAID but moving away is FREE.
#
# WHY. v28 removed the steering cost and the critic recovered (goal Q +21 at
# 400k against v27's -8), but the collapse still came: the ramp reached 0.85
# junction goals at ~440k, training goal success fell 0.44 -> 0.09, and the
# Town02 eval went 0.150 (400k) -> 0.075 (500k).
#
# v28's eval records say the car DRIVES WELL AND THE WRONG WAY: failing
# episodes covered 51 m at 200k and 203-366 m at 400k-500k for returns of -21
# to +3. Lane following is largely solved; choosing the way to the goal is not.
# The signed route term charges every metre driven away, so a car pointed the
# wrong way sees a negative future and a -1 crossing becomes the cheap exit --
# the same cheap-termination mechanism as v27, now driven by wrong-way driving
# instead of the steering cost. It also matches the wrong-goal eval of v18
# (0.600 against 0.725: the image was worth 0.125).
#
# Clipped, the wrong way is merely unpaid: the value of continuing cannot fall
# below zero, ending early stops being attractive, and the only way to score is
# still to reach the goal. gated_reward refuses this flag unless a crossing
# ends the episode, which is what stops approach-retreat being farmed.
. "$REPO/slurm/v28_overlay.env"
export ROUTE_PROGRESS_POSITIVE=1
